One of the only price IDs I ever bother with is the Identify scroll. I
use other ID methods for all other gear:
-Rings, amulets and armour: Find out whether they're cursed and if not,
try them on (Watch out for helmets though- some can auto-curse). If
it's a pair of boots you've tried on, attempt the #jump command. This
won't ID all items, but it will sift out many of them.
-Potions. Dip a dart or arrow into a potion to auto-ID posion or
polymorph. Then dip a unihorn in there to further categorise them.
(Consult spoilers for more details). You can recognise booze and fruit
juice because they are the only potions (apart from water, which is
easy to ID) generated in delicatessens. #dip violet gems into potions
for a chance of IDing booze.
-Wands: Engrave test and, if you have a good idea what it might be, zap
test.
-Scrolls: Watching monsters read them is one good way. Also, if you run
into a scroll in a corridor (and it hasn't been dropped by  monster) or
in a secret cupboard, it's almost certainly teleport.

The trick to IDing everything else is to NEVER read a scroll of ID
unless it's blessed. When you do read one, make sure you have your
inventory full of IDable stuff - even if it means wandering into a
general store, picking everything up, reading your ID scroll and then
dropping all the stuff again. Use ID scrolls wisely. Think very hard
about which items you'd like IDed and which can wait.

You can also get free IDs from thrones sometimes, but thrones can be
perilous to you and your inventory.



